# Machine-local settings for bleck.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Loaded automatically from anywhere inside the checkout -- nothing to source.
# The real environment always wins, so a one-off override still works:
#
#   BLECK_DOLPHIN=/other/Dolphin uv run bleck launch ...
#
# Only BLECK_* names are read from this file. Paths are taken literally, so
# backslashes are safe and quotes are optional (use them for spaces).
#
# Anything left unset falls back to looking on PATH, which is usually right on
# Linux and macOS. Windows generally needs these, because both toolsets ship in
# version-stamped folders nobody wants on PATH.

# --- external tools -------------------------------------------------------

# Wiimms ISO Tool. Extracts and rebuilds discs.
#BLECK_WIT=C:\Users\you\tools\wit\bin\wit.exe

# Wiimms SZS Toolset. Embeds the Gecko loader into the DOL.
#BLECK_WSTRT=C:\Users\you\tools\szs\szs-v2.42a-r8989-cygwin64\bin\wstrt.exe

# The emulator, for `bleck launch` and `scripts/ingame.py`.
#BLECK_DOLPHIN=C:\Users\you\tools\dolphin\Dolphin.exe

# Beside Dolphin.exe. Converts between disc formats.
#BLECK_DOLPHIN_TOOL=C:\Users\you\tools\dolphin\DolphinTool.exe

# PowerPC cross-compiler for code mods. devkitPPC, or a distro cross-gcc.
#BLECK_PPC_GCC=C:\devkitPro\devkitPPC\bin\powerpc-eabi-gcc.exe

# --- inputs that are not shipped -----------------------------------------

# Symbol lists, e.g. spm.eu0.lst. Not vendored: see docs/decision-log.md.
#BLECK_SYMBOLS_DIR=work/symbols

# spm-headers' include tree, if you want game structs in your C.
#BLECK_HEADERS_DIR=work/headers
